          "title": "Kuhn Poker",
          "subtitle": "Vying",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Kuhn Poker is a simplified two-player poker model using only three cards, designed for complete analysis of imperfect-information strategy."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Harold W. Kuhn introduced Kuhn Poker as a zero-sum imperfect-information game suitable for formal game-theoretic analysis."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "2 players use the table arrangement described for Kuhn Poker."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Three-card deck such as king, queen, and jack"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Three-card deck such as king, queen, and jack, score area, and enough table space for play."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Prepare Three-card deck such as king, queen, and jack and deal or lay out cards according to the documented Kuhn Poker rules before play begins."
            }
          ]
